# Editing Historical / Closed Transactions

Current product direction:

Normal users should not modify transactions belonging to locked historical periods.

For exceptional cases, authorized Finance/Admin/Authority-level users may be allowed to perform changes if company policy permits.

Exceptional historical edit/posting must require:

- sufficient authority/permission
- explicit reason
- complete audit trail

The purpose is flexibility for exceptional operational cases while ensuring changes cannot occur silently.

The new architecture should remain configurable enough that management may later choose:

- no override at all; or
- authority-level override with reason/audit.

Detailed period-closing logic belongs to the Accounting capability and is not part of the immediate AR MVP.

Financial Year, Period Closing, and Period Lock are distinct concepts. Creating or selecting a Financial Year does not close or lock it.

