# Revision, Effective Version, Snapshot, and Audit Events

Four concepts must remain distinct.

## Approval / Request Snapshot

Answers: "What exact immutable request payload was submitted or approved at this workflow point?"

For Customer, Submit/Resubmit creates a `MAKER_SUBMISSION` JSONB snapshot. Authority edit-and-approve may create a derived `AUTHORITY_APPROVED` snapshot. A new-Customer snapshot may be complete; an amendment snapshot may preserve only its exact proposed delta/context. Typed Customer revision-child persistence is superseded.

## Effective-dated Version

Answers: "What master value was valid during a defined time range?"

Examples: Company Location and Customer Location address versions. Effective-dated versions are not inferred from audit rows.

## Transaction Snapshot

Answers: "What exact values did the finalized transaction or communication request use?"

Examples include the Customer legal name/GSTIN, Bill-To/Ship-To address, selected credit days/due date, and resolved delivery-recipient value.

## Field-change Evidence

Answers:

"What data changed?"

Example:

Credit Period:
30 → 45

## Business Audit Event

Answers:

"What business action happened?"

Examples:

- Invoice Created
- Invoice Submitted
- Invoice Approved
- Invoice Returned
- Invoice Rejected
- Invoice Edited after approval
- Historical-period override used
- Invoice added to or removed from a draft GSTR-1 filing batch
- GSTR-1 filing batch filed
- Invoice edit blocked because it is included in a FILED GSTR-1 return / filing batch
- E-invoice / IRN generated
- Invoice Email Queued
- Invoice Email Sent
- Invoice Email Failed
- Payment Allocated
- Allocation Changed
- PI Converted to TI
- Exchange Rate Overridden
- Reminder Sent
- Configuration Changed
- GL Account Created / Changed / Inactivated
- Account Hierarchy / Group Relationship / GL Placement Changed
- Revenue GL Mapping Changed
- Tax / Statutory GL Mapping Changed
- Default Receivable GL or Bank GL Association Changed
- Receivable / Revenue / Tax GL Accounts Resolved at Transaction Finalization

